      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لَهُ اَلرَّجُلُ يَتَمَتَّعُ فَيَنْسَى أَنْ يُقَصِّرَ حَتَّى يُهِلَّ بِالْحَجِّ فَقَالَ «عَلَيْهِ دَمٌ».\nوَ فِي رِوَايَةِ عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ بْنِ سِنَانٍ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : «يَسْتَغْفِرُ اَللَّهَ تَعَالَى»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2742 - Ishaq ibn Ammar narrated from Abu Ibrahim (as): I asked him about a man performing tamattu‘ (Hajj) who forgets to trim his hair until he has already entered the state of ihram for Hajj.\nImam (as) said: \"He must offer a sacrifice.\"\nIn another narration, Abdullah ibn Sinan reported from Abu Abdullah (as):\n\"He should seek forgiveness from Allah (swt), the Exalted.\""
        ]
      }
